 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/36f36cd5ece4186095afcf2ffbfb7b80cc04b6c2e3226e7477a419a9fbc96f85.png] **__Key Points__**

__

• **Article 51A**



• Some of the **Fundamental Duties under article 51-A** which should be followed by every Indian citizen are mentioned below:



• to **abide by the Constitution**, its principles, and institutions, as well as the flag and national anthem;

• to respect and support the **noble principles **that motivated our nation's struggle for freedom;

• to safeguard and defend I**ndia's sovereignty, unity, and integrity**;

• to be compassionate toward all living things and to** protect and improve the natural environment**, including forests, lakes, rivers, and wildlife;

• to respect and protect the **rich cultural history of our diverse culture**;





** [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/f13e2ad6582c16aa62a83672e2547ad20a01fddb61962a1acce42eb9a1a99caa.png] Additional Information__**


• **Article 55 **states that** ****Every elected member of a State's Legislative Assembly is entitled to as many votes as there are multiples of 1,000 in the ratio created by dividing the State's population by the total number of elected Assembly members.**

• **Article 48A **states that** The State shall make efforts to protect the country's economic forests and wildlife while also attempting to keep and improve the environment.**

• **Article 52 **states that **There shall be a President of India**.
